  "doc.title": "Why Fermented Tofu Tastes Good · a long essay you can play with",
  "doc.desc": "Tofu has almost no taste, yet mould, salt and a few months make it rich and savoury. A century egg gets somewhere similar with no microbes at all. Seven models you can push: cutting protein chains, two kinds of enzyme, umami synergy, salt and water activity, odour activity values, alkali soaking into an egg, and what you still smell after dilution.",
  "nav.back": "← Knowledge index",
  "nav.lang": "Language",
