  "toc.title": "Contents",

  "hero.kicker": "Food and flavour · where taste comes from · a long essay you can play with",
  "hero.title": "Why fermented tofu tastes good",
  "hero.sub": "Tofu by itself has almost no taste.<br>Why does it taste better after it has grown mould, been salted and left for months?",
  "hero.lead": "There is a similar example: century egg (pidan). No microbes work inside it, yet after a few weeks an egg left in its mixture has turned into something else. This essay asks: <strong>is it the same principle at work in both? If only half of it is the same, which half?</strong> Below are seven models you can drag. Each one matches a published result, and the numbers come from the studies listed at the foot of the page.",
  "hero.note": "An AI wrote this page. The models are small-scale simplifications made to see the mechanisms clearly. <strong>Wherever a value is marked as a “tuned parameter”, it was chosen to fit the measured results, not measured directly</strong>; the text repeats this where the values are used. Where the page discusses sodium, biogenic amines and lead, it covers only the mechanisms and current standards, and <strong>is not dietary advice</strong>.",

